.TH ORO-URL 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:url \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:url'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
oro:url is a JavaScript API module exposed by the Oro Runtime.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBprotocols\fR
Documented variable exposed by this module.
.TP
\fBparse(input, options)\fR
Parse a URL\-like input into a structured object. \- When `options === true`, includes a Node\-compatible `query` object. \- When `options?.strict === true`, returns `null` if input cannot be parsed.
.br
Example: parse('https://user:pass@example.com:8080/a/b?x=1#h') // => { // protocol: 'https:', hostname: 'example.com', origin: 'https://example.com:8080', // username: 'user', password: 'pass', port: '8080', pathname: '/a/b', // search: '?x=1', hash: '#h', path: '/a/b', href: 'https://user:pass@example.com:8080/a/b?x=1#h', // auth: 'user:pass', searchParams: URLSearchParams, query: 'x=1' // }
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIinput\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (boolean \\| URLParseOptions \\| null; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIParsedURL \\| null\fR
.TP
\fBresolve(from, to)\fR
Resolve a target URL/path `to` against a base `from`. Mirrors Node.js `url.resolve()` semantics.
.br
Example: resolve('http://example.com/a/b', '../c') // => 'http://example.com/c' resolve('/a/b', 'c') // => '/a/c'
.TP
\fBformat(input)\fR
Format a URL from either a string or a partial object containing URL fields. Returns an empty string if the input is invalid or insufficient.
.br
Example (object): format({ protocol: 'https:', hostname: 'example.com', pathname: '/a/b' }) // => 'https://example.com/a/b'
.br
Example (string): format('https://example.com/a/b') // => 'https://example.com/a/b'
.br
Notes \- When specifying `hostname` with an IPv6 literal, brackets are added automatically. Alternatively, you can pass `host` directly as `[2001:db8::1]:8080`.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIinput\fR (string \\| URLFormatOptions; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring\fR
.TP
